WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:02.123
<v Examiner>Four marks.

2
00:00:02.123 --> 00:00:06.983
<v Examiner>Explain why clinical documentation is a legal and professional requirement,

3
00:00:06.983 --> 00:00:11.778
<v Examiner>and describe the ISBAR framework for handing over a deteriorating patient.

4
00:00:12.228 --> 00:00:17.394
Documentation is three things: a legal requirement, a professional responsibility,

5
00:00:17.394 --> 00:00:18.969
and a communication tool.

6
00:00:19.419 --> 00:00:23.464
Legal: the Health Practitioners Competence Assurance Act 2003,

7
00:00:23.464 --> 00:00:28.552
which exists to protect the public by making sure practitioners are competent;

8
00:00:28.552 --> 00:00:33.315
the Code of Rights under the Health and Disability Commissioner Act 1994,

9
00:00:33.315 --> 00:00:38.599
where Right one includes having your privacy respected; and the Privacy Act 2020.

10
00:00:38.599 --> 00:00:43.948
Professional: the Nursing Council Code of Conduct, and pou three of the standards,

11
00:00:43.948 --> 00:00:49.558
which says documentation must be legible, relevant, accurate, professional and timely.

12
00:00:49.558 --> 00:00:55.364
And the rule that ties it together: if care isn't recorded, it's assumed it wasn't given.

13
00:00:55.364 --> 00:00:58.169
The healthcare organisation owns the notes.

14
00:00:58.619 --> 00:01:01.160
How to document, for the multi-choice.

15
00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:03.166
A patient label on every page.

16
00:01:03.166 --> 00:01:05.773
Date and time in twenty-four-hour time.

17
00:01:05.773 --> 00:01:08.983
Your name, signature and designation at the end.

18
00:01:08.983 --> 00:01:10.855
Permanent blue or black ink.

19
00:01:10.855 --> 00:01:13.997
No gaps: strike through to the end of the line.

20
00:01:13.997 --> 00:01:18.610
A mistake gets one line through it so the original can still be read,

21
00:01:18.610 --> 00:01:21.017
then sign it and note it's an error.

22
00:01:21.017 --> 00:01:22.087
Never white-out.

23
00:01:22.087 --> 00:01:26.700
No generalisations like condition unchanged, no judgemental language,

24
00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:30.244
and use correct terms: write cyanosis, not blue lips.

25
00:01:30.694 --> 00:01:32.612
Now ISBAR, with its extra R.

26
00:01:32.612 --> 00:01:36.036
I, identify: yourself, your role, and the patient.

27
00:01:36.036 --> 00:01:38.843
S, situation: what's happening right now.

28
00:01:38.843 --> 00:01:42.747
B, background: why they came in and the relevant history.

29
00:01:42.747 --> 00:01:48.842
Letter A, assessment: vital signs, anything outside normal, and your clinical impression.

30
00:01:48.842 --> 00:01:53.499
For example, temperature thirty-nine point three and she's confused.

31
00:01:53.499 --> 00:01:57.334
R, recommendation: what you need done, and how urgently.

32
00:01:57.334 --> 00:02:00.484
And R, review: what happened after the action.

33
00:02:00.934 --> 00:02:06.365
The other framework is SOAP, or SOAPIER: subjective, objective, assessment, plan,

34
00:02:06.365 --> 00:02:08.913
intervention, evaluation and revision.

35
00:02:09.363 --> 00:02:15.436
Documentation is legal, the H P C A Act, the Code and the Privacy Act; professional,

36
00:02:15.436 --> 00:02:19.267
the Code of Conduct and pou three; and communication.

37
00:02:19.267 --> 00:02:21.436
Not documented means not done.

38
00:02:21.436 --> 00:02:25.196
Blue or black ink, no gaps, one line through errors.

39
00:02:25.196 --> 00:02:30.618
ISBAR: identify, situation, background, assessment, recommendation, review.

40
00:02:30.618 --> 00:02:36.763
SOAPIER: subjective, objective, assessment, plan, intervention, evaluation, revision.
